cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CORAL in your research, please cite this software and the associated publication."
title: "CORAL: Coral reef Optimization for Adaptive Layouts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zondervan"
    given-names: "Edwin"

version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-19

abstract: >-
  CORAL is a topology-aware coral-reef-inspired optimization algorithm
  for mixed-integer chemical process superstructure optimization. It
  combines structural exploration, feasibility-first settlement,
  adaptive search operators, diversity preservation, bleaching and
  recolonization, and optional local nonlinear-programming refinement.

keywords:
  - optimization
  - process systems engineering
  - process synthesis
  - superstructure optimization
  - mixed-integer nonlinear programming
  - metaheuristics
  - coral reef optimization
  - MATLAB

license: MIT
